; Stage 15 W8 G-4 (design/global-init.md §4.2): a `defvar` initializer that
; SYNTACTICALLY names a global whose own `defvar` has not been reached yet is a
; compile error, and the diagnostic names BOTH sites — the reference, and the
; declaration it is waiting on.
;
; Initializers run in the order their `defvar` forms are reached during
; emission, so `g4-fwd-a` would run while `g4-fwd-b` still held its zero and
; `g4-fwd-a` would silently be 1 instead of 42. Swapping the two forms is the
; whole fix; `run_g4_order` links and runs that version and asserts 42.
(defn g4-fwd-compute ():i32 (return 41))

(defvar g4-fwd-a:i32 (+ g4-fwd-b 1))
(defvar g4-fwd-b:i32 (g4-fwd-compute))

(defn main ():i32 (return g4-fwd-a))
